	I finished it a couple of days back. Didn't have much trouble.
	I used the first wand to wish for scrolls of charging, blessed
luckstone, Mjollnir, speed boots and amulet of life saving.
	The shop not only had two WoW, but also two WoP !!

	Polymorphed for gray dragon scale mail. I don't know if the luckstone
had anything to do with it but, the WoW in the castle started of with 3
wishes ! Very nice (not that I needed it!). 

	Genocided all Liches and rust monsters.

	I didn't have a potion of paralysis, but I had intrinsic teleport,
teleport control and enough food (those C and K-rations are indispensable).
So I teleported to each stairway and didn't meet him till Level 1. What
surprised me was that he followed me into the endgame. I didn't think the
Wiz. would go to Level -1.


	That's about it I guess. As far as stats, the high score was around
1.7 million points, I had +7 Excalibur and Mjollnir(dumped the rest of 
artifacts before going to Hell), 2 amulets of life saving, several wands,
rings of conflict, teleport control, polymorph control, +3 speed boots, shield
of reflection, +0 gray dragon scale mail, +3 gauntlets of dexterity, 
+2 Hawaiin shirt, +1 orcish helm, +1 cloak of displacement plus unicorn horn,
blindfold, skeleton key, blessed luckstone.


Possible Spoilers______________








	Try a wand of sleep on a Minotaur. 

	Giving gold to a co-aligned priest helps a lot. I found something
interesting - It is (in my opinion) better to go for the "blessing" than for 
the AC bonus. If you get enough "blessings", you have intrinsic clairvoyance
which lasted me the whole game (even the endgame). Very helpful, when you
are in Hell, because it maps the level out for you and helps a lot in
finding the stairways. I ahd to move around a bit, teleport to a few diff.
locations and I would have the whole level mapped out !!

	While giving gold to the priest, I tried out the leprechaun scam. 
It works very easily. Waht makes it even better - As a leprechaun, you can
HIT the Priest without pissing off the deity !!! I don't know if it reduces
your luck, but with a blessed luckstone, I don't think it would matter. All
it needs is a little patience, and you can have AC's of -100 !!!
        I think this needs to be changed !! The game should keep track of
your polymorphs and if you hit the Priest after polymorphing into a 
leprechaun, it should piss the deity off and possibly take away a few
intrinsics or maybe levels.


